# PROBE inverse-properties. s is r's inverse, so A ⊑ ∃r.B and B ⊑ ∀s.C entail A ⊑ C.
# construct: InverseObjectProperties
# expect: sub :A :C
# expect-not: sub :B :C

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:A a owl:Class . :B a owl:Class . :C a owl:Class .
:r a owl:ObjectProperty . :s a owl:ObjectProperty .
:s owl:inverseOf :r .
:A rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :r ; owl:someValuesFrom :B ] .
:B rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :s ; owl:allValuesFrom :C ] .
